\par\par \uc2 National Desk; SECTA\par \b \uc2 Thousands Go On Strike In Los Angeles\b0\par\par\uc2 By Jill Cowan \par \uc2 691 \uc2 words\par \uc2 9 August 2023\par \uc2 The New York Times\par \uc2 NYTF\par \uc2 Late Edition - Final\par 14\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 Copyright 2023 The New York Times Company.  All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 Municipal workers walked out on Tuesday to draw attention to widespread understaffing.\par \par \uc2 The News\par \par \uc2 Thousands of municipal workers in Los Angeles walked off the job for one day on Tuesday to demand that city leaders address widespread staffing shortages that have stretched employees thin.\par \par \uc2 The walkout was expected to snarl a range of city operations, including trash collection and services at \uc2 Los Angeles International Airport\uc2 . City officials emphasized that the city would not shut down, and as of Tuesday afternoon, impacts appeared to be limited.\par \par \uc2 Los Angeles mayor Karen Bass said in a statement on Tuesday that ''city services were impacted, but continued.''\par \par \uc2 Because the city runs \uc2 Los Angeles International Airport\uc2 , shuttle bus drivers, bus mechanics and custodians are participating in the one-day strike. City officials had warned those headed to the airport to build an extra hour into their travel plans, but as of Tuesday afternoon, traffic was flowing normally to the terminals.\par \par \uc2 Why It Matters\par \par \uc2 The strike comes amid what California labor leaders have called a ''hot labor summer,'' during which a wave of walkouts and strikes have been spurred by frustration over wages that they say haven't kept pace with the sky-high costs of living in Los Angeles and with inflation.\par \par \uc2 Hollywood writers and actors are on strike together for the first time in decades. Hotel workers across the region have been picketing in waves since the long July 4 weekend.\par \par \uc2 Labor officials have said that workers in a wide range of fields -- crane operators at the port, custodians at public schools and more -- understand what it's like to struggle to make ends meet in a region where housing costs and other living expenses continue to soar.\par \par \uc2 David Green, the president and executive director of the union that represents the city employees, said that roughly 11,000 workers, including members of other unions, were expected to join picket lines at City Hall, Griffith Observatory and other locations.\par \par \uc2 Background\par \par \uc2 The union, \uc2 Service Employees International Union\uc2  Local 721, organized the walkout on Tuesday to protest what it considers to be unfair labor practices by the city, Mr. Green said. Contract negotiations broke down in the spring, he said, after the city sent negotiators who were not authorized to close deals. Union members feel that the city is not approaching the staffing crisis with sufficient urgency.\par \par \uc2 In the city's sanitation department alone, according to Mr. Green, more than 900 jobs are open and there are scores of additional vacancies in other city departments. He said that the office that processes job applications was also severely understaffed, and that it often took six months or more to respond to applicants, who by then had found other jobs.\par \par \uc2 ''There's no immediacy,'' he said. ''But if you're our members, there's immediacy -- if you're working mandatory overtime every weekend, if you haven't seen your family.''\par \par \uc2 In a statement, Ms. Bass said that the city had been bargaining with Local 721 in good faith since January.\par \par \uc2 ''The city will always be available to make progress 24 hours a day, seven days a week,'' Ms. Bass, a Democrat, said.\par \par \uc2 What's Next\par \par \uc2 Trash pickup was expected to be delayed by a day through the rest of the week, and the city was planning to rely on contractors for sewer-related emergencies.\par \par \uc2 Ms. Bass said that the city's transportation department was slated to execute contingency plans for managing traffic around the Greek Theatre, where the young singer and songwriter Dominic Fike was scheduled to play a show on Tuesday night, and the Hollywood Bowl, which was set to host the Los Angeles Philharmonic. She added that there were similar plans for BMO Stadium, the home of the Los Angeles Football Club, who were scheduled to play Real Salt Lake.\par \par \uc2 Many services, including child care and summer camps, were uninterrupted, the mayor said.\par \par \uc2 A bargaining session is scheduled for Monday, a spokesman for the union said. The union's contract expires at the end of the year.\par \par \uc2 This article appeared in print on page A14. \par \par \uc2 Document NYTF000020230809ej890004a\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw284\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal4260\pichgoal600
