\par\par \uc2 Business/Financial Desk; SECTB\par \b \uc2 Even Zoom Is Returning To the Office\b0\par\par\uc2 By Emma Goldberg \par \uc2 943 \uc2 words\par \uc2 8 August 2023\par \uc2 The New York Times\par \uc2 NYTF\par \uc2 Late Edition - Final\par 4\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 Copyright 2023 The New York Times Company.  All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 The tech company that helped millions of people work from home is finally tired of its employees being far away. It's not the only one that feels that way.\par \par \uc2 During the early months of the pandemic, a certain company went suddenly from relative obscurity to the type of popularity that made it a noun, verb and catchphrase.\par \par \uc2 ''Can you set up a Zoom for us?''\par \par \uc2 ''Let's just Zoom.''\par \par \uc2 ''I have Zoom fatigue.''\par \par \uc2 Revenue for the video conferencing company soared in 2020 -- a jump driven by the millions of people who started working from home. Zoom was also part of the remote work shift that it powered, with most of its employees permitted to work from home.\par \par \uc2 But now, joining a swell of other tech firms pushing for in-person work, Zoom is requiring many of its 7,400 employees to start showing up at the office.\par \par \uc2 The company last week asked all employees within 50 miles of an office to work in person on a part-time basis, a plan Zoom said it would roll out in August and September.\par \par \uc2 ''We believe that a structured hybrid approach -- meaning employees that live near an office need to be on site two days a week to interact with their teams -- is most effective for Zoom,'' a company spokesperson said. ''We'll continue to leverage the entire Zoom platform to keep our employees and dispersed teams connected and working efficiently.''\par \par \uc2 During a tense meeting last week about the return to office policy, held on Zoom, \uc2 Eric Yuan\uc2 , the chief executive, faced a series of questions from employees who expressed frustration about the time and money they'd waste while commuting, according to an employee who was at the meeting but was not authorized to speak publicly about internal company matters.\par \par \uc2 In 2020, participants in daily Zoom meetings leaped to over 300 million, from 10 million the year before, as it became the most downloaded free iPhone app of the year. But the company has struggled to maintain its pandemic growth. In February, amid a wave of layoffs across the tech industry, Zoom cut 15 percent of its staff, or about 1,300 people. The company's work force had grown more than 275 percent between July 2019 and October 2022.\par \par \uc2 On an earnings call in May, Mr. Yuan said he was confident in the future of workplace flexibility and the benefits it had brought for his company. ''I think hybrid work is going to stay,'' he said.\par \par \uc2 Zoom, like many other tech companies, is still holding on to some flexibility, requiring its employees to come in only on a part-time basis.\par \par \uc2 Hybrid and remote work levels remain far above what they were prepandemic. As of July, nearly one-third of the country's full-time workers were in hybrid arrangements, spending some days working from home and some in an office, according to researchers at Stanford.\par \par \uc2 But dozens of companies have joined Zoom in tightening their policies on office attendance this summer, as offices remain at just under half of their prepandemic occupancy levels.\par \par \uc2 Google\uc2 , which has asked employees to come into the office three days a week, announced that managers could take unexcused absences from the office into account when doing performance reviews and could use badge records to identify those absences. \uc2 Salesforce\uc2 , taking a softer approach, said it would give a $10 charitable donation per day on behalf of any employee who came into the office for a 10-day period in June.\par \par \uc2 Many companies have faced fierce resistance as they call people back to the office. Hundreds of \uc2 Amazon\uc2 's corporate employees walked off the job for an hour in May, protesting the company's announcement that they had to return to the office at least three days a week. At \uc2 Apple\uc2 , corporate employees signed petitions protesting their return to the office.\par \par \uc2 At the start of the pandemic, the tech industry was quick to embrace flexible work, which was enabled by the industry's own products, including \uc2 Slack\uc2  (owned by \uc2 Salesforce\uc2 ), Gmail and Zoom.\par \par \uc2 But many of those companies realized that they didn't want their employees to remain permanently scattered. Nick Bloom, a Stanford economist and expert on hybrid work, said the tech industry's move back to the office was no surprise given the amount these companies spend on office real estate.\par \par \uc2 Mr. Bloom said Zoom, for example, had all the downsides of fully remote work -- some employees feeling disconnected -- without the company seeing its financial upsides, like saving money on office space, because the company was still paying for Bay Area real estate and Bay Area employees.\par \par \uc2 ''They're paying for their office and hiring local people so they get no upside from being fully remote,'' Mr. Bloom said. ''The most surprising thing to me was they took so long to formally announce this.''\par \par \uc2 Recent studies have confirmed some benefits to in-person work. A working paper released earlier this year from economists at the \uc2 Federal Reserve Bank of New York\uc2 , the \uc2 University of Iowa\uc2  and Harvard found that at one tech firm, remote work decreased the amount of feedback that junior employees received on their work. Researchers from the \uc2 Massachusetts Institute of Technology\uc2  found that remote work at M.I.T. led to a 38 percent decline in ''weak ties,'' meaning the loose connections that help advance people's careers.\par \par \uc2 Still, more than 90 percent of workers who can do their jobs remotely now want some flexibility in where they work, according to Gallup.\par \par \uc2 This article appeared in print on page B4. \par \par \uc2 Document NYTF000020230808ej880004k\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw284\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal4260\pichgoal600
